WEBVTT

00:00:00.415 --> 00:00:03.573
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.573 --> 00:00:05.951
Being together like this...

00:00:05.951 --> 00:00:09.829
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.829 --> 00:00:13.250
Forever...

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.752
...under this sky...

00:00:15.752 --> 00:00:18.046
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.756 --> 00:00:21.049
In this beauty...

00:00:21.049 --> 00:00:22.175
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:23.218
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:24.344
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.636 --> 00:00:25.971
With more dreaming...

00:00:25.971 --> 00:00:27.055
...and more loving...

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:28.139
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.139 --> 00:00:29.349
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:30.600
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.019
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:35.689
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:37.899
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.610
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.654
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.654 --> 00:00:45.365
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:47.492
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.492 --> 00:00:50.578
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:56.418
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.418 --> 00:00:58.753
If you go there...

00:00:58.753 --> 00:01:02.757
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.757 --> 00:01:06.136
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.136 --> 00:01:08.596
Under this sky...

00:01:08.596 --> 00:01:10.974
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.021
Being together like this...

00:01:16.021 --> 00:01:19.524
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:25.739
Under this sky...

00:01:25.739 --> 00:01:27.991
...we'll walk together!

00:01:39.973 --> 00:01:41.141
Thank you very much.

00:01:41.266 --> 00:01:44.103
No problem! The stories you
made up were great fun.

00:01:44.728 --> 00:01:45.771
M Uh, those weren't...

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.148
Yeah, yeah. See ya!

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.199
<i>Right now, I'm in Karuizawa.</i>

00:01:58.158 --> 00:02:01.161
I'm not here for fun, but to investigate a case.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:04.998
<i>I was playing around on a computer at DDS...</i>

00:02:04.998 --> 00:02:07.835
<i>...and found an open case amongst the jobs
Dan Detective Agency had taken on.</i>

00:02:08.168 --> 00:02:11.588
<i>It was called "Karuizawa - Murdered
Idol in a Sealed Room".</i>

00:02:12.881 --> 00:02:16.468
<i>It’s about a girl who was aiming
to become a movie star,</i>

00:02:16.677 --> 00:02:19.346
<i>...and how she mysteriously died
in a completely sealed roam.</i>

00:02:19.847 --> 00:02:27.062
<i>I was intrigued and wanted to solve this puzzle
alone, so I 'm using my days off to come here.</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.321
So this is it.

00:02:37.281 --> 00:02:39.408
Now where's the crime scene?

00:02:43.203 --> 00:02:44.163
Excuse me.

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:49.751
There it is.

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:55.048
I guess it's locked...

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.635
Hmm... What should I do?

00:02:58.635 --> 00:02:59.511
Hey!

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:00.929
I'm sorry!

00:03:04.141 --> 00:03:05.684
What are you freaking out about, Kyuu?

00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:08.896
Yukihira? What are you doing here?

00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:13.901
I was watching you look through the case files.

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:14.902
Why?

00:03:15.652 --> 00:03:17.905
Well that's because I'm interested in you.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.742
Well, isn't it kinda sudden to...

00:03:21.825 --> 00:03:23.660
No, silly. That's not what I meant.

00:03:24.453 --> 00:03:27.831
I'm interested in your detective skills.

00:03:28.457 --> 00:03:32.294
That's why I asked DDS for permission
to be this case's supervisor.

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:34.880
So you can become a case
supervisor just by asking?

00:03:35.255 --> 00:03:36.757
In any case, you've come.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:37.799
Huh?

00:03:38.091 --> 00:03:40.552
Kyuu, I'm challenging you.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.430
Who can solve this case first?

00:03:44.348 --> 00:03:45.057
It's a contest!

00:03:45.515 --> 00:03:47.059
What? Why?

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:47.976
Because.

00:03:49.436 --> 00:03:54.358
Ah, so that's what it's about. I guess
I'll just do my thing, as always.

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:00.155
We're here from DDS.

00:04:00.656 --> 00:04:01.865
I'm Sakurako Yukihira.

00:04:02.449 --> 00:04:04.451
My name's Kurita, nice to meet you.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.079
I'm Kyuu, nice to meet you too.

00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:12.000
That's enough.

00:04:12.876 --> 00:04:18.382
According to the request form, your sister,
Sumika, was a participant in this event, too, right?

00:04:18.382 --> 00:04:19.341
Yes.

00:04:20.175 --> 00:04:25.430
This film festival is being held to promote
Kyouhou Studios' fortieth anniversary movie.

00:04:26.139 --> 00:04:30.811
We're touring the whole country in six months...

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:35.565
...and holding a vote to pick
the lead in the movie.

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.110
That means you're all rivals.

00:04:38.402 --> 00:04:40.070
Yes, and...

00:04:40.737 --> 00:04:43.532
...it was almost certain that my sister would win.

00:04:44.574 --> 00:04:45.284
That's why...

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.786
She was killed out of jealousy.

00:04:48.787 --> 00:04:49.913
There's no doubt about it.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.292
There was even a threat letter.

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:55.377
Do you still have it?

00:04:57.337 --> 00:04:57.879
Here you go.

00:05:00.799 --> 00:05:06.680
The room my sister died in was completely
sealed, so the police suspect it's an accident.

00:05:07.222 --> 00:05:09.683
But I can't help thinking it was something else.

00:05:12.019 --> 00:05:15.981
I beg you, please find my sister's killer!

00:05:17.774 --> 00:05:19.276
Please come in quickly!

00:05:19.818 --> 00:05:21.278
The show is about to start.

00:05:21.778 --> 00:05:25.866
The girl over there is Momoko Tachikawa,
the youngest of the five. .

00:05:27.117 --> 00:05:30.787
She's seventeen and dropped out of
high school to participate here.

00:05:31.455 --> 00:05:32.622
What, seriously?

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:36.335
Seventeen that's the same age
as you, Yakihira, and yet...

00:05:38.545 --> 00:05:39.463
What about her?

00:05:40.964 --> 00:05:42.758
That's Nagisa Takamura

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:46.094
She's just returned to the country and
is a daughter of a rich family.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.891
Wow, she's fluent in English

00:05:50.974 --> 00:05:52.392
Bah, it's not like I don't speak English.

00:05:53.602 --> 00:05:56.146
What about the woman standing on
the stage, under those balloons?

00:05:56.521 --> 00:05:58.023
That's Natsumi Yamazaki.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.400
Hi everybody.

00:06:00.442 --> 00:06:02.069
She's twenty on paper, but...

00:06:03.862 --> 00:06:06.573
Wow! Look at those long legs!

00:06:06.782 --> 00:06:08.283
Hey, Reika.

00:06:08.784 --> 00:06:10.410
Ah, Mr. Obi.

00:06:10.869 --> 00:06:11.828
\ . " ' ;
Where have you been? -

00:06:12.329 --> 00:06:14.122
You left your booth without telling anyone.

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:15.332
I'm sorry.

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:17.376
It's about my sister.

00:06:18.668 --> 00:06:19.336
I see

00:06:20.128 --> 00:06:23.173
But right now, you're the next
in line for the lead role.

00:06:24.174 --> 00:06:25.258
Please give it your all.

00:06:27.886 --> 00:06:29.262
So he's your manager.

00:06:30.514 --> 00:06:32.140
These are all the people involved, then?

00:06:32.724 --> 00:06:33.600
Y-Yes

00:06:34.142 --> 00:06:36.269
Then let's take a look at the crime scene.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:40.107
It'll be alright.

00:06:46.154 --> 00:06:46.947
It's open already?

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.827
Wow, it's tiny and completely bare.

00:06:52.244 --> 00:06:54.204
Sleeping here must be rough...

00:06:54.913 --> 00:06:57.582
So, the door was bolted shut from the inside.

00:06:57.958 --> 00:06:59.000
Y-Yes...

00:06:59.793 --> 00:07:01.628
It's a lot sturdier than I'd expected.

00:07:02.462 --> 00:07:08.343
And with this door impossible to lock the
bolt from the outside using a wire or thread.

00:07:09.469 --> 00:07:12.222
There doesn't seem to be any other
way in, except the door.

00:07:15.475 --> 00:07:17.310
The window was open the entire time?

00:07:18.478 --> 00:07:21.189
But it's too narrow for a person to fit through.

00:07:21.898 --> 00:07:27.279
If this were really a murder, it means that it
was a murder in a completely sealed room.

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:31.116
Hey Manager, how come you still
haven't gotten us a hotel room?

00:07:31.741 --> 00:07:35.537
I'm sorry Nagisa, but everything's completely
booked due to the long weekend.

00:07:36.037 --> 00:07:38.123
And our budget's very tight as well.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:39.416
Are you kidding me?

00:07:39.833 --> 00:07:43.044
You're telling me to sleep in this
cursed place again tonight?

00:07:43.545 --> 00:07:44.754
Cursed?

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:48.550
The police confirmed that Sumika's death
was an accident caused by sleeping pills.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:51.219
No, it was definitely a curse!

00:07:51.887 --> 00:07:53.472
Sumika was killed...

00:07:53.763 --> 00:07:55.098
...by Misuzu Hikawa's curse.

00:07:57.309 --> 00:07:58.226
Nagisa...

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.020
Anyway, I'm scared!

00:08:00.353 --> 00:08:02.022
Wait, let's talk about it...

00:08:03.398 --> 00:08:06.067
Reika, who's this Misuzu Hikawa?

00:08:08.987 --> 00:08:12.240
Actually, there was another girl that died
in an accident three months ago.

00:08:14.075 --> 00:08:16.578
Someone else died before your Sister?

00:08:17.329 --> 00:08:19.915
Excuse me, I'll tell you about this later.

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:30.175
I see.

00:08:31.551 --> 00:08:33.553
Beautiful roses have sharp thorns.

00:08:35.388 --> 00:08:37.265
It looks like there's a lot going on
that we don't know about yet.

00:08:38.475 --> 00:08:39.851
I wonder what's up with Reika.

00:08:40.393 --> 00:08:43.063
Kyuu, let's each investigate on
our own from here on out.

00:08:43.688 --> 00:08:44.606
What? Why?

00:08:45.232 --> 00:08:45.899
Didn't I tell you?

00:08:46.608 --> 00:08:49.819
This is a match between us,
with our pride on the line.

00:08:50.904 --> 00:08:51.279
See ya.

00:08:52.781 --> 00:08:53.573
Yukihira...

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.828
I'm Yukihira from DDS.

00:08:59.621 --> 00:09:03.750
I've received an order to investigate the case
regarding the death of Sumika Kurita.

00:09:04.292 --> 00:09:06.461
DDS? That famous...

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.547
Why would someone like you...

00:09:09.089 --> 00:09:10.006
Oh, please have a seat.

00:09:10.298 --> 00:09:11.007
Thank you.

00:09:14.427 --> 00:09:18.640
According to the police, it was an accident.

00:09:19.182 --> 00:09:21.351
It's a little too early to assume that.

00:09:22.602 --> 00:09:24.896
I believe a new investigation is necessary.

00:09:25.939 --> 00:09:27.065
Could I ask for your assistance?

00:09:27.774 --> 00:09:30.110
Of course, if there's anything I can do.

00:09:30.694 --> 00:09:37.242
Then what kind of person was Misuzu Hikawa,
and how did she die three months ago?

00:09:37.534 --> 00:09:38.159
Ah, yes...

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:48.253
Misuzu was a little pretentious, but she
was the most popular until she died.

00:09:49.421 --> 00:09:52.299
She died during the event in the Northeast.

00:09:53.258 --> 00:09:58.221
There was a rumor that there
was a ghost in our hotel.

00:09:58.888 --> 00:10:02.434
Misuzu was easily-frightened and
wasn't happy about staying there.

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:04.394
On the second night...

00:10:07.939 --> 00:10:11.359
...we all rushed to see what made her
scream, and discovered her dead...

00:10:11.359 --> 00:10:14.696
...after hitting her head on the rocks
underneath the outdoor bath.

00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:19.159
After Misuzu, Sumika died...

00:10:20.493 --> 00:10:23.204
Maybe it really is a curse.

00:10:23.538 --> 00:10:25.332
Maybe this event, itself, is cursed...

00:10:27.584 --> 00:10:29.377
Wow that really happened?

00:10:29.794 --> 00:10:31.379
Yeah, isn't that scary?

00:10:31.796 --> 00:10:34.883
But Momo, I'm amazed you keep on
going, despite what's happened.

00:10:35.592 --> 00:10:36.926
I don't have any other options.

00:10:37.552 --> 00:10:41.931
I mean, I dropped out of high school, that's
why I'm going to get that role in the movie.

00:10:42.182 --> 00:10:42.849
I see.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.144
I'm not the only one.

00:10:46.936 --> 00:10:48.188
Everybody's desperate.

00:10:49.314 --> 00:10:51.691
I think that they'd do anything
to get the lead role.

00:10:53.234 --> 00:10:55.945
By the way, why do you have a sleeping bag?

00:10:59.574 --> 00:11:00.408
Are you sure it's alright?

00:11:00.909 --> 00:11:03.036
Of course, just stay over.

00:11:03.787 --> 00:11:05.497
Just don't do anything perverted.

00:11:06.831 --> 00:11:07.791
Like I would.

00:11:07.999 --> 00:11:08.583
This is it.

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:11.961
Please come in!

00:11:12.128 --> 00:11:13.046
Momoko.

00:11:13.963 --> 00:11:14.964
Mr. Ooi!

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:17.342
I'm walking around, just in case.

00:11:19.594 --> 00:11:22.722
Geez, you can't just stay in a girl's room.

00:11:24.182 --> 00:11:28.269
By the way, weren't you with Ms.
Yukihira from DDS earlier?

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:31.064
Yes, I just met her recently.

00:11:31.064 --> 00:11:33.775
Could you wait here for a second?

00:11:35.151 --> 00:11:35.777
Reika?

00:11:36.486 --> 00:11:37.904
Yes? It's open.

00:11:40.323 --> 00:11:42.450
What's wrong? You look tired.

00:11:43.118 --> 00:11:44.577
My allergies are bogging me down a little.

00:11:45.286 --> 00:11:47.914
But I'm going to talkie my medicine
and get a good night's sleep.

00:11:48.123 --> 00:11:48.707
Okay, good.

00:11:49.624 --> 00:11:52.293
Then, please lock the door and the dead bolt.

00:11:52.752 --> 00:11:54.295
Have a good night, Reika.

00:11:56.089 --> 00:11:56.506
Yes.

00:11:58.633 --> 00:12:01.386
I can't believe you came here without
even having a place to stay.

00:12:01.678 --> 00:12:02.429
I'm sorry.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.516
I'm telling you now, try anything
funny and you're dead meat.

00:12:06.975 --> 00:12:07.684
Funny?

00:12:08.143 --> 00:12:08.935
Just go to sleep.

00:12:15.608 --> 00:12:16.609
Hey, Yukihira.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:19.237
What is it?

00:12:20.196 --> 00:12:21.489
Isn't something bugging you?

00:12:22.657 --> 00:12:25.326
About our client, Reika Kurita?

00:12:26.786 --> 00:12:28.413
Leave it for tomorrow.

00:12:34.169 --> 00:12:34.878
But...

00:12:35.253 --> 00:12:35.920
What?

00:12:37.255 --> 00:12:40.258
I got the feeling that she was really scared.

00:12:43.428 --> 00:12:45.138
Somehow, it keeps bugging me.

00:12:47.724 --> 00:12:50.477
Geez, it's 2 AM.

00:12:50.935 --> 00:12:52.687
That's why I said I'd go alone.

00:12:52.812 --> 00:12:54.105
That wouldn't be okay, either...

00:12:54.731 --> 00:12:55.273
Something's weird!

00:12:55.982 --> 00:12:56.649
Wait.

00:13:03.031 --> 00:13:04.032
This doesn't look right.

00:13:05.533 --> 00:13:06.785
I can't hear her breathe...

00:13:08.703 --> 00:13:09.746
...and her chest isn't moving.

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.791
She couldn't be... dead!

00:13:20.022 --> 00:13:20.564
She couldn't be...

00:13:21.607 --> 00:13:22.108
She's...

00:13:22.733 --> 00:13:23.234
Reika!

00:13:23.859 --> 00:13:24.527
Reika!

00:13:24.944 --> 00:13:25.403
Damn it!

00:13:25.486 --> 00:13:26.028
Kyuu!

00:13:27.571 --> 00:13:29.698
Momo, please wake up, Memo!

00:13:36.789 --> 00:13:38.290
Damn it, it's locked!

00:13:38.707 --> 00:13:40.793
Move, I'll open the lock.

00:13:44.672 --> 00:13:48.008
It's no good, I opened the lock but
the dead bolt's still in place.

00:13:48.342 --> 00:13:49.927
It's just like when something
happened to Sumika.

00:13:50.678 --> 00:13:51.303
We gotta bust it open!

00:13:51.804 --> 00:13:52.888
One, two, three!

00:13:54.223 --> 00:13:56.058
It's no good, it's not budging

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.102
We can't give up, one more time.

00:13:58.436 --> 00:13:59.520
One, two, three!

00:14:05.693 --> 00:14:09.238
She stopped breathing but her
heart's still beating faintly.

00:14:13.868 --> 00:14:16.036
What are you doing? Call an ambulance, quick!

00:14:16.162 --> 00:14:17.455
Ah, of course!

00:14:22.418 --> 00:14:26.255
Who would have thought that someone
from DDS would be the first to find her.

00:14:27.256 --> 00:14:28.883
I'm Sakurako Yukihira.

00:14:29.675 --> 00:14:33.429
I'm here to investigate yesterday's incident.

00:14:34.847 --> 00:14:36.307
Would you be so kind as to assist me with that?

00:14:37.141 --> 00:14:38.017
Of course.

00:14:39.393 --> 00:14:40.769
And who might you be?

00:14:41.562 --> 00:14:45.774
I'm from my middle school's mystery
. club and randomly met her.

00:14:45.774 --> 00:14:47.401
Why are you still hiding it?

00:14:48.027 --> 00:14:53.282
Uh, there's some stuff I'd like him to help me
with, I hope you don't mind him tagging along.

00:14:55.784 --> 00:15:00.414
Mr. Ooi, are you certain that Ms. Reika's
medicine was for her allergies?

00:15:00.414 --> 00:15:01.540
0

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.126
Well, that's what she said...

00:15:04.752 --> 00:15:05.920
Is that so...

00:15:06.629 --> 00:15:08.756
Actually, I gave her that medicine.

00:15:09.673 --> 00:15:13.177
My allergies are quite bad, so
I've got quite a selection.

00:15:14.803 --> 00:15:19.266
I gave her the strongest I have, but I didn't
put any poison in it or anything like that.

00:15:19.391 --> 00:15:22.811
Allergy medicine makes you
really tired, doesn't it?

00:15:23.812 --> 00:15:24.605
Excuse me.

00:15:25.356 --> 00:15:26.190
Nagisa...

00:15:26.857 --> 00:15:28.609
I heard something happened to Reika!

00:15:28.984 --> 00:15:33.197
Where have you been at this time
of night, Ms. Nagisa Takamura?

00:15:33.697 --> 00:15:40.454
I was just at a park close by because I wanted to
read the script to the upcoming movie out loud.

00:15:41.539 --> 00:15:43.832
Ms. Nagisa, you're pretty quick to the draw.

00:15:44.625 --> 00:15:48.462
A Are you thinking that all your rivals will
disappear, leaving you to get the lead role?

00:15:48.837 --> 00:15:49.630
How dare you!

00:15:50.506 --> 00:15:51.465
Please calm down.

00:15:51.632 --> 00:15:56.387
More importantly, Ms. Takamura, is there anyone
that can testify you were practicing at the park?

00:15:56.637 --> 00:16:00.474
Of course there's nobody like that.
But I've got the script right here.

00:16:01.016 --> 00:16:02.142
Please let me take a look.

00:16:09.108 --> 00:16:14.363
It looks like you sent Sumika Kurita
a threatening letter recently.

00:16:16.282 --> 00:16:19.493
Nagisa did? How do you know?

00:16:20.202 --> 00:16:21.954
Please take a look at this script.

00:16:22.913 --> 00:16:25.165
Alongside each kanji is its reading.

00:16:26.709 --> 00:16:29.003
I did that because Nagisa has been
living in the US her whole life.

00:16:29.461 --> 00:16:33.257
She can speak well enough,
but she can't read kanji.

00:16:34.049 --> 00:16:35.467
So what's that supposed to prove?

00:16:37.845 --> 00:16:41.223
Please take a close look at this threat letter
made up of these cut out print letters.

00:16:41.932 --> 00:16:45.185
Only the kanji are cut out very
closely to the right edge.

00:16:45.811 --> 00:16:48.272
You're right. But what does
that have to do with...

00:16:48.397 --> 00:16:49.231
You don't see it?

00:16:50.316 --> 00:16:54.737
These are kanji that were cut gut from
text with the reading written next to it.

00:16:57.156 --> 00:16:58.991
Isn't that right, Ms. Takamura?

00:17:00.659 --> 00:17:03.162
That's nothing more than conjecture.

00:17:04.288 --> 00:17:07.541
Besides, aren't the issues surrounding
Reika more important right now?

00:17:10.085 --> 00:17:14.006
I mean, I'm sure it was an
accident or some illness.

00:17:15.049 --> 00:17:18.719
Or maybe it's the curse of the
late Misuzu Hikawa after all.

00:17:26.352 --> 00:17:29.063
I guess that means you didn't
make any progress either.

00:17:29.813 --> 00:17:30.314
Here you go.

00:17:30.648 --> 00:17:31.649
Thank you very much!

00:17:34.777 --> 00:17:37.946
Yukihira, Reika's okay, right?

00:17:38.906 --> 00:17:42.201
I'm not sure. She'd stopped
breathing for a while, and...

00:17:43.702 --> 00:17:45.120
I hope she wakes up soon.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:52.920
Hey, when you saw her last night, she said
she was taking allergy medicine, right?

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.672
Yes.

00:17:54.672 --> 00:18:01.804
I'm sure the perpetrator used the medicine
to plan a sealed room murder.

00:18:02.471 --> 00:18:03.847
Then the perpetrator is...

00:18:04.765 --> 00:18:06.642
Someone who knows about the medicine.

00:18:07.768 --> 00:18:09.436
The perpetrator must be among them!

00:18:12.439 --> 00:18:16.568
Yukihira, there's something else on my mind.

00:18:17.236 --> 00:18:18.112
Something on your mind?

00:18:19.405 --> 00:18:20.155
It's the smell.

00:18:21.448 --> 00:18:25.160
When we entered Reika's room,
there was a bad smell.

00:18:26.245 --> 00:18:28.038
Something like burning plastic.

00:18:28.789 --> 00:18:32.376
Are you saying that that smell has some sort
of connection to the sealed room murder?

00:18:32.793 --> 00:18:34.753
Hmm... I'm not sure.

00:18:35.337 --> 00:18:37.381
But it sorta keeps bugging me.

00:18:37.631 --> 00:18:39.425
You're strange after all.

00:18:40.175 --> 00:18:44.471
Getting your mind stuck on irrelevant stuff,
hiding the fact that you're from DDS...

00:18:45.472 --> 00:18:47.641
Headmaster Dan told us to.

00:18:49.685 --> 00:18:50.728
That's Something my uncle would say.

00:18:51.812 --> 00:18:52.312
Uncle?

00:18:52.855 --> 00:18:59.153
Yup, even within DDS only a select few know
about this, but Morihiko Dan's my uncle.

00:19:01.905 --> 00:19:07.494
For the record, getting into DDS and making it
into the A Class is the result of my hard work.

00:19:08.579 --> 00:19:12.708
My uncle has always been against
me becoming a detective...

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.501
Really?

00:19:15.294 --> 00:19:22.468
Of course, but I believe that I'm the only one
who can be Morihiko Dan's successor.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:25.971
Good morning.

00:19:25.971 --> 00:19:27.139
Thanks for coming.

00:19:27.139 --> 00:19:28.140
What?

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.601
They're still carrying on with the event even
though something like that happened?

00:19:33.604 --> 00:19:35.147
Good morning!

00:19:36.607 --> 00:19:39.985
Welcome to the Kyouhou Movie Theater!

00:19:41.779 --> 00:19:42.613
That's a lot of smoke.

00:19:43.113 --> 00:19:46.450
Thank you for coming here
this early in the morning.

00:19:47.868 --> 00:19:48.577
This is it.

00:19:48.827 --> 00:19:51.330
I figured out how you could suffocate someone
in a completely scaled room.

00:19:55.501 --> 00:19:58.879
Ms. Yukihira, I gathered all
the people involved. But...

00:19:59.004 --> 00:20:00.005
Thank you.

00:20:00.506 --> 00:20:04.343
I'm going to replicate the trick used to
' suffocate someone in a sealed room.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:05.928
What did you say?

00:20:07.054 --> 00:20:11.600
In this box we have dry ice that
was used at the show just now.

00:20:13.936 --> 00:20:15.103
What's this about?

00:20:15.479 --> 00:20:19.149
To put it simply, the perpetrator
filled the room with C02...

00:20:19.358 --> 00:20:25.155
...released by dry ice to
suffocate Sumika and Reika.

00:20:26.073 --> 00:20:27.115
This is how it was done.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:30.452
After the perpetrator confirmed
the victim was asleep...

00:20:30.786 --> 00:20:35.833
...he dropped large quantities
of dry ice through the window.

00:20:36.917 --> 00:20:41.463
As C02 is heavier than air, in a closed
room, it'll accumulate on the floor.

00:20:42.172 --> 00:20:46.885
However, the victim, in deep sleep
because of the medicine...

00:20:47.177 --> 00:20:49.513
...won't wake up and suffocates
from the lack of oxygen.

00:20:50.806 --> 00:20:54.601
Please watch, in a little while
this candle should go out.

00:20:55.853 --> 00:20:57.479
Just as one would expect from DDS.

00:20:59.231 --> 00:21:00.941
<i>I’ve won, Kyuu.</i>

00:21:03.485 --> 00:21:08.115
Um, It's been more than half an
hour but it's not going out.

00:21:08.782 --> 00:21:10.033
And isn't it cold on top of that?

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:14.496
Of course it is if you have such a
large quantity of dry ice around.

00:21:15.372 --> 00:21:16.123
Yukihira...

00:21:16.623 --> 00:21:18.208
What? It's just a matter of seconds now.

00:21:18.709 --> 00:21:19.334
But look at that.

00:21:22.504 --> 00:21:26.383
Isn't the air in this place constantly
circulated through those vents?

00:21:27.926 --> 00:21:30.846
Yes, I think it's an automatic all-day system.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.015
That can't be...

00:21:33.765 --> 00:21:34.600
That means...

00:21:35.517 --> 00:21:37.060
It has to be something else.

00:21:37.811 --> 00:21:43.108
If it had been C02, it means that there would
have been a lot left when we entered the room.

00:21:44.026 --> 00:21:46.653
Then there would have been
smoke, like at the show.

00:21:47.613 --> 00:21:49.656
And the biggest hint would
be the air temperature.

00:21:50.782 --> 00:21:53.243
It looks like you've over thought it.

00:21:53.911 --> 00:21:54.786
Let's go.

00:21:55.662 --> 00:21:57.623
What a waste of time. Let's go.

00:22:03.378 --> 00:22:07.716
Yukihira, let's start from square one, together.

00:22:10.344 --> 00:22:11.762
Our match isn't over yet!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:14.014
Yukihira...

00:22:17.643 --> 00:22:21.939
But it's a fact that two people
were suffocated here.

00:22:24.316 --> 00:22:28.946
Ah yes, it's times like this when I have to consult
my bible, "The detectives Notebook".

00:22:33.116 --> 00:22:36.745
In these situations you "won't notice something
out of place by only looking at one thing".

00:22:37.579 --> 00:22:39.414
So I gotta go compare.

00:22:41.708 --> 00:22:42.918
Momo, I'm coming in.

00:22:43.585 --> 00:22:45.671
Wait, I'm trying on my bathing suit right now!

00:22:49.675 --> 00:22:51.093
See if there are any differences.

00:22:51.635 --> 00:22:53.303
Compare every square inch.

00:22:55.555 --> 00:22:59.434
Momo, I don't see anything.

00:23:00.519 --> 00:23:02.312
I'm sorry for being flat!

00:23:04.022 --> 00:23:05.315
Oh... are you okay?

00:23:07.275 --> 00:23:09.528
I see! I've got it, that's it!

00:23:11.822 --> 00:23:12.531
I'm not going to lose!

00:23:13.657 --> 00:23:15.492
I'm going to solve this case!

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.662
The first place to search
for evidence is the trash.

00:23:19.454 --> 00:23:20.122
Maybe...

00:23:24.418 --> 00:23:26.253
What... is this?

00:23:28.588 --> 00:23:29.381
I've almost got it.

00:23:31.466 --> 00:23:32.676
Almost.

00:23:35.971 --> 00:23:37.014
Why's something like this here?

00:23:45.509 --> 00:23:47.344
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.344 --> 00:23:49.680
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.349
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.349 --> 00:23:54.018
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.018 --> 00:23:56.020
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.020 --> 00:23:58.314
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.314 --> 00:24:00.858
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.858 --> 00:24:02.651
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:06.906
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.906 --> 00:24:10.534
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.577 --> 00:24:13.621
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.621 --> 00:24:16.040
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.040 --> 00:24:18.167
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.167 --> 00:24:19.710
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.169 --> 00:24:22.379
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.379 --> 00:24:24.590
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:26.800
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:30.304
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.096 --> 00:24:33.265
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.265 --> 00:24:35.184
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.184 --> 00:24:37.561
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.603 --> 00:24:40.397
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:25:07.645 --> 00:25:09.272
I've got a bad feeling.

00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:11.482
Maybe something happened to those two.

00:25:12.191 --> 00:25:12.900
Where?

00:25:13.234 --> 00:25:14.360
Where are they?

00:25:16.237 --> 00:25:17.280
It's Gedzilla!

00:25:17.280 --> 00:25:18.197
Gedzilla tripped!

00:25:18.614 --> 00:25:19.699
Let's sit on him!

00:25:19.866 --> 00:25:21.784
This disguise might have been a bad pick...
